#  DBMS External Examination Preparation – Day 1

Today, I am officially starting my preparation for the **Database Management Systems (DBMS) External Examination** as part of my MCA journey.

My goal is not just to prepare for university examinations but also to develop strong conceptual knowledge of DBMS for technical interviews and real-world software development.

###  Learning Objectives
- Understand DBMS fundamentals and architecture.
- Learn different types of database models.
- Understand ER diagrams and relational models.
- Master SQL queries from basic to advanced.
- Practice SQL constraints, keys, and relationships.
- Learn relational algebra and relational calculus.
- Understand functional dependencies and normalization.
- Explore transactions, ACID properties, concurrency control, and recovery.

###  My Learning Approach
- Daily concept revision.
- Hands-on SQL practice using MySQL.
- Solving university examination questions.
- Maintaining notes and practical examples.
- Regularly uploading my learning progress to GitHub.

###  Goal
Build a strong foundation in DBMS that supports both academic excellence and future placement preparation.

**Starting today, one concept, one practical session, and one step forward every day!**

